	The main guide to changing the Nethack code is German
Martin's writeup on how to change Nethack, which is the top link at:
http://members.shaw.ca/rob.ellwood/HowToChangeNethack.html

	He stopped before getting as far as adding new character
classes.  Still, he has documented a lot of the sub-steps (adding
new monsters and objects) and I've covered a few more (adding new
tiles).

	In Section 9.2 of "Making New Levels" (3rd link above), I 
documented what I know about creating new classes.  (Or, more 
accurately, what Dylan knew.)  The first paragraph starts:

        "Adding a new class might take 40 hours of work.  Less for
professional programmers, more if you have no coding skills."

	Some of the work can be done by other people.  (e.g.:  Kelly
Bailey or I could do the quest levels.)  No-one else is likely to do
the programming.

	Two works in progress might help you:

   o  Nephi offered to write up what he has learned.

   o  I'm writing a "how to change Nethack" course.  It is oriented
      towards non-programmers using Windows.  (If you're interested
      in this, say.  I'm only likely to finish it if someone says
      'can I have a copy by mid-month?')  I'm afraid that the course
      won't give you all the skills you need to do something this
      big.  You'll have to get a reference book on C and periodical-
      ly ask for help. 


